Third-party software used at run time (not included in this repository)
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
update_anyps5.py downloads these on the user's machine, from their authors'
official repositories. They are run as separate programs (or read as data, e.g.
setting names in the source and documentation) and are not distributed with or
linked into this tool.

AnyPS5 - https://github.com/boykopovar/AnyPS5
  Author: boykopovar and contributors
  License: GNU General Public License, version 2 only.
  Downloaded: the source tree of the main branch (AnyPS5-main/);
    tools/unwrap_self.py, tools/import_audit.py, tools/nid_names.py, tools/progress.py;
    the release assets relinker-<version>.exe and prx-windows-<version>.zip.
  Setting descriptions in anyps5_settings.py and docs/SETTINGS.md summarise the
  AnyPS5 documentation (docs/user/USAGE.md, docs/user/INPUT_MAPPING.md).

PS5-SELF-TO-ELF - https://github.com/julienlgy/PS5-SELF-TO-ELF
  Author: julienlgy
  License: none published at the time of writing (all rights reserved by the author).
  Downloaded: self_to_elf.py from the latest commit of the default branch, into tools/.
  Because no license grants redistribution, this repository never contains a copy of
  it; each user fetches it directly from the author's repository.

The AnyPS5 Windows libraries ship the MinGW-w64 runtime DLLs (libgcc_s_seh-1.dll,
libstdc++-6.dll, libwinpthread-1.dll) under their own licenses.

